A cone-shaped pile of sand has a base diameter of $12\text{ m}$ and a slant height of $10\text{ m}$. Find the perpendicular height of the pile.

mastery.solution_text:
First halve the diameter to get the base radius.
$r=12\div2=6\text{ m}$
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[scale=0.900]
\coordinate (P) at (0,0);
\coordinate (Q) at (2.400,0);
\coordinate (R) at (0,3.200);
\draw (P)--(Q)--(R)--cycle;
\draw (0.28,0)--(0.28,0.28)--(0,0.28);
\node[below] at (1.200,0) {$6\text{ m}$};
\node[left] at (0,1.600) {$h$};
\node[above right] at (1.200,1.600) {$10\text{ m}$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
The slant height is the hypotenuse, so the perpendicular height is a shorter side.
$h=\sqrt{10^{2}-6^{2}}$
$=\sqrt{64}$
$=8\text{ m}$

